**How to implement.** Both Launcher buttons, Main and Inverse, open the kit start screen, and the launcher's own kit opening goes (001 §F 'Both Launcher buttons, Main and Inverse, open the start screen'; 001 §O 'Launcher: Main / Inverse / Materials / Library. Main and Inverse open the kit start screen'; the S5.2 brief: Main and Inverse open the start screen instead of the picker, and Materials and Library are unchanged; .spec-md §4: superseded code is deleted in the change that replaces it). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`. (a) After `InverseConstructorWindow`, `module private KitConstructorWindows` holds `showConstructorIn (context : AppContext) (mode : ConstructorMode) (opened : OpenedKit) : unit`, showing `MainConstructorWindow(context, opened)` for `ForwardConstructor` and `InverseConstructorWindow(context, opened)` for `InverseConstructor`, step 154's mode match moved out of the launcher's local function; its doc is one line. (b) `LauncherWindow(locations, settings, opened, pickerFor)` keeps its signature (steps 88, 89, 112, 154). Main's click shows `KitStartWindow(context, ForwardConstructor, pickerFor, KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn context)` (step 179), and Inverse's the same with `InverseConstructor`; each click opens one start screen. The launcher's kit opening is deleted whole: step 154's local function of the folder, the mode and the access, the `launcherKitErrorText` block, step 155's holder line with its Open read-only / Cancel row, and their calls of `pickThen`, `resolveAndShow`, `openFailedCaption` and `openElsewhereCaption` (steps 173, 174), whose callers are now the start screen alone. Materials, Library, the library error, the Recreate library button and the pending-imports notice (steps 88, 89, 112) are unchanged, because they need no kit (001 §F). The docs of `LauncherWindow`, `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` say, in no more words, that Main and Inverse open the start screen and that a window works in the kit the start screen opened. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group: `launcherKitErrorText`, `launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton` and `launcherCancelKitOpenButton` (steps 154, 155) are deleted with their docs; the start screen's `kitStartStatusText`, `openKitReadOnlyButton` and `cancelKitStartOfferButton` (step 178) replace them. (3) Tests. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs`, each fact that clicked Main or Inverse to open a kit observes the one `KitStartWindow` the click opens (through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent`, as `clickAndObserve` does) and then presses the start screen's box that the old fact reached through the launcher, at its centre as `LauncherTests.fs:clickBorder` presses one; the launcher's picker (`fun _ -> TestAppScope.kitPickerOf …`, step 154) is the start screen's picker. `the Main button opens the forward Main constructor scene` and `the Inverse button opens the inverse constructor scene`: the click opens exactly one `KitStartWindow`, titled `Open a kit — Main` (`Open a kit — Inverse`); pressing its `newKitButton` opens exactly one `MainConstructorWindow` (`InverseConstructorWindow`), closes the start screen, and leaves `.kit-json` in the fresh folder. `the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments`: through the start screen's `openKitButton`, every assertion kept. `a cancelled pick opens nothing`: pressing `newKitButton` with a picker answering `None` opens no constructor window, creates no folder and keeps the start screen open. `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the launcher and opens no window` is renamed `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the start screen and opens no window`: pressing `openKitButton` shows `kitStartStatusText` naming `E1.experiment-json`, opens no constructor window and leaves no `.oc/lock`. `acceptance: a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only and Cancel in one row, and Open read-only opens it without writing` and `Cancel on a kit open elsewhere opens nothing`: through `openKitButton`, the holder's line is `kitStartOfferText` and the pair `openKitReadOnlyButton` / `cancelKitStartOfferButton`, every assertion kept. `acceptance: a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first, and Apply opens the constructor over its library`, `cancelling a kit's import dialog opens nothing and releases the kit` and `a kit whose snapshots the library holds byte for byte confirms every reuse row before opening`: through `openKitButton`, every assertion kept, and Cancel on the dialog keeps the start screen open. `Materials from the launcher then the constructor strip activates ONE single instance` and every Materials, Library, library-error, recreate and pending-import fact keep their code. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`: `the launcher and both constructor states render over ONE root-composed app scope` also shows, asserts and closes `KitStartWindow(ctx, ForwardConstructor, …)` and `KitStartWindow(ctx, InverseConstructor, …)` over the same context, with a picker of a fresh folder and a `showConstructor` that ignores its kit, so ui-smoke renders the screen in both modes. `WireUiCompositionTests` and `WireUi0040CompositionTests` build their constructor windows directly (step 154) and keep their code; `SmokeTests.fs` keeps its code, because `App.OnFrameworkInitializationCompleted` (`Program.fs:App`) builds the launcher as before. Afterwards `git grep -n -F -e launcherKitErrorText -e launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton -e launcherCancelKitOpenButton -- Berreman/` finds nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the Launcher is re-wired, its Main and Inverse buttons MUST each open a `KitStartWindow` of their mode whose chosen kit opens the matching constructor window, Materials and Library MUST be unchanged, and `git grep -n -F -e launcherKitErrorText -e launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton -e launcherCancelKitOpenButton -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the Main button opens the forward Main constructor scene`, `the Inverse button opens the inverse constructor scene`, `the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments`, `a cancelled pick opens nothing`, `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the start screen and opens no window` (renamed from `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the launcher and opens no window`), `acceptance: a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only and Cancel in one row, and Open read-only opens it without writing`, `Cancel on a kit open elsewhere opens nothing`, `acceptance: a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first, and Apply opens the constructor over its library`, `cancelling a kit's import dialog opens nothing and releases the kit`, `a kit whose snapshots the library holds byte for byte confirms every reuse row before opening` and `the launcher and both constructor states render over ONE root-composed app scope`, the count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.
